{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0663"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge art/architecture","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/art__architecture.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",802],["+","An alcove is a recess opening off a room, and above all the windowless niche that held a bed: in the town houses and farmhouses of the 17th to 19th centuries people went into the alcove to sleep, often behind a curtain or a pair of doors. The word came into French and German from the Spanish alcoba, \"bedroom\", which goes back to the Arabic al-qubba, \"the vault\".\n\n"],["=",107],["+","\n| alcove | windowless niche for a bed |"],["=",3],["-","five"],["+","six"],["=",54]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",738],["+","Ein Alkoven ist ein Nebenraum, der sich zu einem Zimmer öffnet, vor allem die fensterlose Nische, in der ein Bett stand: In den Bürger- und Bauernhäusern des 17. bis 19. Jahrhunderts zog man sich zum Schlafen in den Alkoven zurück, oft hinter einem Vorhang oder einer Doppeltür. Das Wort kam aus dem spanischen alcoba, „Schlafzimmer“, ins Französische und Deutsche und geht auf das arabische al-qubba, „das Gewölbe“, zurück.\n\n"],["=",97],["+","\n| Alkoven | fensterlose Bettnische |"],["=",3],["-","fünf"],["+","sechs"],["=",54]]}]},
